# RingCheck's safeguards (D43, D165): one mutant per safeguard per
# implementation, Ring.swift (s-) and ring.h (c-). RingCheck's memory
# model keeps loads in program order, so an acquire load or fence is a
# no-op to it, and the consumer's release store (its copies are loads)
# can't be shown needed; those survive, each saying so. Safeguards the
# model threads never reach (argument and header validation, hostile
# cursors, a stream's trailing bytes) are caught by the sequential tests
# in RingModelTests.swift, which run on both implementations.
suite RingCheckTests
